- BOTTOM-LEFT: Edge quality badge → thin line points to the edge/border
- BOTTOM-RIGHT: Comfort/benefit badge → general product
- BOTTOM-CENTER: Set info badge → "${pieceInfo.split(',').length || 6} Parça Set"

Badge style: Small rounded rectangle, white background with subtle drop shadow, dark text, clean modern sans-serif font. Connected by thin (1px) straight lines to the product.

Badge text suggestions (ALL IN TURKISH — choose what fits this product):
1. Fabric: "Pamuk Saten" / "Ranforce" / "Keten" / "%100 Pamuk"
2. Feature: "El İşi Nakış" / "Jakarlı Desen" / "Dijital Baskı"
3. Edge: "Çift Dikiş Kalite" / "Pipo Kenar" / "Nakışlı Kenar"
4. Benefit: "Nefes Alan Doku" / "Yumuşak Tüşe" / "4 Mevsim" / "Antialerjik"
5. Set: piece count info

CRITICAL:
- Product must match reference images exactly.
- ALL text must be in TURKISH with correct characters (ş, ğ, ü, ö, ç, ı, İ).
- ${ar} aspect ratio.`,
  },
  {
    id: "color_texture_ref",
    label: "Renk/Doku Referans",
    group: "C",
    description: "Nakış ve kumaş detay çekimi — pastel arka plan",
    textFirst: true,
    enabled: true,
    promptBuilder: (_gp, sig, _pi, ar) =>
`Aesthetic close-up photograph showing fabric texture and embroidery detail of the bedding product from the reference images.

PRODUCT DETAILS: ${sig}

COMPOSITION: Show a section of the duvet/nevresim surface laid at a slight angle (~30°), with 1-2 stuffed pillows partially visible in the soft background. The embroidery/pattern area must be the HERO — tack sharp, centered, filling most of the frame. The fabric should lay naturally with gentle folds showing its weight and character.

BACKGROUND: Soft muted pastel surface/backdrop — Bella Maison catalog style. Choose a pastel that CONTRASTS with the product color:
- If product is green/sage → warm blush pink or soft peach
- If product is blue/navy → warm sand or dusty pink
- If product is white/cream → sage green or dusty rose
- If product is pink/rose → soft sage or cool light grey
- If product is earth/brown tones → muted blue-grey or soft lavender
UNIFORM, FLAT, MATTE surface — no texture, no marble, no grain.

CAMERA: Slightly elevated angle (~35-40°), close to the fabric surface. Shallow depth of field — embroidery area sharp, pillows in background soft bokeh. Warm natural light.

CRITICAL:
- This is NOT a flat swatch on white. It's an AESTHETIC lifestyle detail shot showing fabric quality and embroidery craftsmanship.
- Product colors, embroidery, and edge treatments must match references exactly.
- No text, no watermarks.
- ${ar} aspect ratio.`,
  },
];

export type PipelineCallback = (progress: PipelineProgress) => void;

export async function runPipeline(
  referenceImagesBase64: string[],
  generationPrompt: string,
  signatureDetails: string,
  aspectRatio: string,
  enabledShotIds: string[],
  userNotes: string,
  pieceInfo: string,
  onProgress: PipelineCallback
): Promise<PipelineResult[]> {
  const shots = PIPELINE_SHOTS.filter((s) => enabledShotIds.includes(s.id));

  const results: PipelineResult[] = shots.map((s) => ({
    id: s.id,
    label: s.label,
    imageUrl: null,
    status: "pending" as const,
  }));

  const updateProgress = (group: "A" | "B" | "C" | "done", shotId: string) => {
    onProgress({
      currentGroup: group,
      currentShot: shotId,
      completedCount: results.filter((r) => r.status === "done").length,
      totalCount: results.length,
      results: [...results],
    });
  };

  const userContext = userNotes
    ? `\n\nCONTEXT FROM USER (for accuracy only, do NOT render as text): ${userNotes}`
    : "";
  const fullGenerationPrompt = generationPrompt + userContext;
  const fullSignatureDetails = signatureDetails + userContext;

  // Fully sequential — one shot at a time, model gets full attention per shot
  for (const shot of shots) {
    const idx = results.findIndex((r) => r.id === shot.id);
    results[idx].status = "generating";
    updateProgress(shot.group, shot.id);

    try {
      const prompt = shot.promptBuilder(fullGenerationPrompt, fullSignatureDetails, pieceInfo, aspectRatio);
      const imageUrl = await generateImageRaw(prompt, referenceImagesBase64, aspectRatio, shot.textFirst);
      results[idx].imageUrl = imageUrl;
      results[idx].status = "done";
    } catch (err: any) {
      results[idx].status = "error";
      results[idx].error = err.message || "Uretim hatasi";
    }
    updateProgress(shot.group, shot.id);
  }

  updateProgress("done", "");
  return results;
}
